### 1. Login as SUPERADMIN
# @name superadminLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "superadmin",
  "password": "SuperAdmin123!"
}

### 2. Register a fresh test user to promote
# @name registerFutureAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "futureadmin",
  "email": "futureadmin@example.com",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}

### 3. List admins (should be empty at first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admins
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 4. Promote futureadmin to ADMIN
# @name promoteUser
POST http://localhost:8080/api/admins/{{registerFutureAdmin.response.body.userId}}/promote
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 5. Grant MANAGE_PRODUCTS permission to the new admin
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/admins/{{registerFutureAdmin.response.body.userId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminLogin.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "activity": "MANAGE_PRODUCTS",
  "grant": true
}

### 6. Confirm the permission shows up in the admin list
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admins
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 7. Login as futureadmin to get their own token
# @name futureAdminLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "futureadmin",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}

### 8. Try listing admins AS futureadmin - should fail (403), they lack MANAGE_ADMINS
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admins
Authorization: Bearer {{futureAdminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 9. Try listing admins with NO token at all - should fail (401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admins

### 10. Public endpoint - list activities (no auth needed)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/activities